    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the access point during low-visibility or nighttime responses.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the driveway to maintain clear passage for emergency vehicles along its full length.\n• Cut back dense vegetation growing close to the structure to keep a clear path for responders moving around the building.\n• Clear a designated turnaround area near the residence so fire and emergency vehicles can reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the perimeter fence gate unlocked or install a knox-box style lock so responders can access the property without delay.\n• Mark the fence gate location with a reflective sign or marker visible from the driveway approach.\n• Remove or trim any landscaping that narrows the driveway width, particularly at turns, to allow large emergency vehicles to pass without obstruction.\n• Identify and mark a secondary staging area on the open terrain where additional responding units can park without blocking the primary access drive."
  },
