    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or within a few feet of the structure.\n• Thin the tree cluster nearest to the structure to create open space between individual trees and the building.\n• Remove low-hanging branches from scattered trees near the structure so flames cannot climb from ground vegetation up into the tree canopy.\n• Cut or mow grass cover close to the structure down to a short height, particularly during dry months.\n• Clear brush from the area immediately surrounding the structure to reduce the amount of burnable material close to the building.\n• Trim overhanging branches along the driveway so fire vehicles and equipment can pass through without obstruction.\n• Cut back shrubs and brush growing along the driveway edges to reduce the chance that roadside vegetation ignites and blocks access.\n• Mow or cut grass along the driveway corridor to keep low growth from spreading fire across the access route.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway passable by removing any vegetation that narrows the travel lane."
